    "updated_at": "2024-10-10T15:58:01Z",
    "body": "FWIW, during TPAC the [Screen Capture Community Group](https://www.w3.org/groups/cg/sccg/) also explored the idea of adding a \"sensitive\" attribute for the purpose of capture warning/prevention to protect user privacy:\r\n- [Capture Prevention For Privacy Protection](https://www.w3.org/events/meetings/b059a6cc-ac2a-482b-a9e2-32f72c6beb60/)\r\n- [Slides](https://drive.google.com/file/d/17eYulAihsQC7eCzKZZtxUiTrPddHdZpz/view)\r\n\r\nThe idea is similar, if the page/element contains sensitive information (banking account, medical record), then user may want to think twice before capturing and sharing the page.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
